1. What this licence covers

"BA" means the work of the BA project itself: the ba_tts code, its configuration files
(including ba_config.json), the text normalisers and their lexicons, the documentation and
model card, the audio samples, and the BA name, logo and other brand assets.

It does not cover third-party components. They keep their own licences (section 7).

2. What you may do

If you follow the conditions below, you may, free of charge and for non-commercial purposes:
  a. use BA;
  b. modify BA;
  c. share BA and your modified versions.

This licence does not let you use the BA name or logo to suggest that your work is BA or is
endorsed by its owner, beyond the attribution required below.

3. Conditions

  a. Attribution. Keep this licence and the copyright notice with every copy, say that your
     work is based on BA, and link to https://huggingface.co/mahmoudalyosify/BA. If you changed
     BA, say so.
  b. Same terms. Share BA and anything you derive from it only under this licence.
  c. Non-commercial. Commercial use needs the copyright holder's prior written permission.
     Commercial use means use for, or as part of, anything sold, licensed, or offered for
     money or other paid benefit, including paid services and advertising-funded products.
     To ask for permission, contact the owner through the Hugging Face profile
     https://huggingface.co/mahmoudalyosify.

4. Voices and consent

You may only use a voice with BA if you are that speaker, or if you have that speaker's
explicit permission to clone their voice and to use it the way you intend.

5. Forbidden uses

You may not use BA, or anything made with it:
  a. to impersonate anyone;
  b. for fraud, scams or deception, including making people believe a real person said
     something they did not say;
  c. to harass, threaten, defame or bully anyone;
  d. to create sexual, intimate or otherwise harmful content with someone's voice without
     their consent, or any non-consensual content;
  e. to break the law.

6. Watermark

BA puts an inaudible watermark in the audio it produces. Do not remove, alter, or try to
circumvent it, and do not help others do so. Do not publish or give to others BA audio made
with the watermark switched off.

7. Third-party components

BA runs together with components made by others. Each keeps its own licence:
  - VoxCPM2 model weights (OpenBMB): Apache License 2.0. The weights in the BA model
    repository are unmodified; see LICENSE-VoxCPM2 and NOTICE.
  - Whisper large-v3-turbo (OpenAI), used to transcribe reference recordings: MIT License.
  - AudioSeal (Meta), the watermark model and code: MIT License.
  - Other software packages BA depends on: their own licences.

Nothing in this licence restricts any right that those licences give you. You may use the
VoxCPM2 weights, Whisper and AudioSeal under their own licences, independently of BA. This
licence adds conditions only to BA's own work.

8. Ending this licence

If you break this licence, your rights under it end automatically. They come back if you
fix the breach within 30 days of learning about it, unless the copyright holder has already
told you in writing that they will not.

9. No warranty

BA is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The authors are not liable for any
claim, damage or other liability arising from BA or from its use. You are responsible for how
you use BA and for the audio you make with it.
